course: dictionary
lesson: 814
title: Behind: place, race and left
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Behind is a small word with several jobs. Often it tells you where something is: «a stripy head, with high shoulders behind it» means the shoulders are at the back. Behind can also mean after someone in a line or a race, or left in a place.
explain: The words around behind give you the clue. In «I left my bag behind», nothing comes after behind, and it means the bag was not taken with you. In «Always close farm gates behind you», behind points to the back of you as you pass through, so the gate stays shut for the animals.
explain: Behind can also mean late or slower than others, as in «behind with homework». Ask yourself: is something at the back, is someone losing, or was something left? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Behind means at the back of something, as in «behind the tree».
fact: Behind can mean after someone in a line or a race. A runner behind is losing.
fact: Behind can mean late or slower than others, as in «fall behind».
fact: Behind can mean left in a place, as in «left behind».
fact: Behind can be a preposition (it is followed by a noun, as in «behind the tree») or an adverb (it stands alone, as in «I left my bag behind»).
exercise: «Always close farm gates behind you so animals cannot escape.» What does behind mean here? | Under the gate, out of sight | Before you arrive | *At the back of you, once you have passed through | Far away from the farm
exercise: Jayden is losing every race this term. Which word shows he is losing? | term | every | race | *behind
exercise: «I left my bag behind.» What does behind mean here? | *Left in a place, not taken with you | Carried very carefully | Found again after a long search | At the back of the bag
test: «The cat hid behind the sofa.» Where is the cat? | Under the table | Out in the garden | *At the back of the sofa | On top of the cushions
test: Mina is behind with her homework, so she stays in at break. What does behind mean? | Happy and relaxed | *Late, or not finished yet | Early and ahead of everyone | Lost in the playground
exam: In «I left my bag behind», what kind of word is behind? | *Adverb, because it stands alone with no noun after it | Adjective, because it describes the bag | Verb, because it shows an action | Noun, because it names something
